    "checks": [
      "The zoning code has no accessory dwelling unit, accessory apartment or in-law rule. R-C and R-S list single-family detached dwellings and accessory uses 'and no other' (602, 702)",
      "Only one principal use is allowed on a lot in R-C, R-S and R-T (1729)",
      "A use 'clearly not permitted by this Chapter in any zoning district' may be permitted as a conditional use (1726). A second unit is not such a use: two-family dwellings are permitted in R-T and conversion apartments are defined (202, 802). The path for a second unit in R-C and R-S is a use variance. 1726 is at most a question to ask for a detached unit",
      "Two-family detached dwellings are permitted in R-T at 6,000 sq ft per dwelling unit with public water and sewer (802, 805). In this code a 'two family detached' dwelling has one unit 'wholly or partly above the other' (202). R-T density is at most six units per acre (806)",
      "A conversion apartment is defined (202) but the district parts read list none for R-C, R-S or R-T. Section 1801 applies only 'If otherwise allowed as a permitted use'",
      "Accessory buildings may not be in a required yard except the rear yard, 10 ft from the rear lot line (1810.5)",
      "Parking: two spaces for each family unit in a one- or two-family dwelling (2002.A(1))",
      "R-S lot size depends on utilities: 10,000 sq ft with public water and sewer, 12,500 with sewer only, 30,000 without public sewer (705). R-C: 30,000 with public sewer, 40,000 without (605)",
      "Open space development lots (1820): accessory uses in the rear yard only, 10 ft from the rear line, 15 ft high"
    ],
